nueFromContractWithCustomerIncludingAssessedTax","l":"Revenue from Contract with Customer, Including Assessed Tax","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"}},"co_fcf":null,"co_status":"no_release","co_errors":0,"co_tried":1}},"dims_ytd":{"2026-03-31":{},"2026-06-30":{}},"keep":7,"hist":2,"profile":{"cik":1851491,"name":"AMASS BRANDS","tickers":["AMSS"],"exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sic":"2080","industry":"Beverages","sector":"consumer-staples","fye":"1231","state":"DE","category":"<br>Emerging growth company"},"intro":{"text":"AMASS Brands, Inc.(Nasdaq: AMSS) is a next-generation beverage platform built around the brands defining how modern consumers drink, and increasingly, how they don\u2019t. The company\u2019s portfolio spans non-alcohol, functional, and alcohol 2.0 categories, with standout brands across each: Good Twin Non-Alcoholic Wine, a top non-alcoholic wine in the U.S. and one of the fastest-growing in the category; AMASS Electrolytes, a functional disruptor redefining the hydration category; and Summer Water Ros\u00e9, the zero-sugar, #1-selling domestic ros\u00e9 priced between $15 and $20 in the U.S., among others across the portfolio. As moderation trends accelerate, AMASS is positioned to benefit structurally rather than reactively, with margin discipline, cohesive brand architecture, and the multi-brand scalability that supports the Company\u2019s long-term brand and platform growth strategy.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851491/000157587226000675/amss045_ex99-1.htm","filed":"2026-10-06","source":"8-K"},"periods":{"q":["2025-03-31","2025-06-30","2026-03-31","2026-06-30"],"fy":[]},"da_v":2,"quality":{"v":6,"unit":"USD","q":[{"end":"2025-03-31","start":null,"label":"Q1 2025","ni":-3719621,"basis":"pl","ocf":-720777,"assets_open":null,"assets_close":null,"wc":{"rev":4340544,"cor":3125784,"days":91,"ar_o":null,"ar_c":null,"inv_o":null,"inv_c":null,"ap_o":null,"ap_c":null,"ap_proxy":false,"has_inv":true,"dso":null,"dio":null,"dpo":null,"ccc":null},"bridge"